        {
          "path": "_m/d/p/0/4/lincoln-tomb-wp/lincoln-tomb-7167048461.jpg",
          "filename": "Lincoln Tomb (7167048461).jpg",
          "caption": "The Lincoln Tomb in Springfield, a national landmark (1865). It is the final resting place of Lincoln and most of his immediate family (Robert Todd Lincoln is buried in Arlington Cemetery). Lincoln died on April 15, 1865, and a group immediately formed in Springfield to honor Lincoln with a tomb. Lincoln's body went on a nationwide tour--it is estimated that more people saw Lincoln dead than alive. His body returned to Springfield on May 3, and after laying in state for a day at the Old Illinois State Capitol, it was moved to a vault in Oak Ridge Cemetery. His body was finally moved to the tomb in 1871, though it would not be completed until 1874.",
          "alt": "The Lincoln Tomb in Springfield, a national landmark (1865). It is the final resting place of Lincoln and most of his immediate family (Robert Todd Lincoln is buried in Arlington Cemetery). Lincoln died on April 15, 1865, and a group immediately formed in Springfield to honor Lincoln with a tomb. Lincoln's body went on a nationwide tour--it is estimated that more people saw Lincoln dead than alive. His body returned to Springfield on May 3, and after laying in state for a day at the Old Illinois State Capitol, it was moved to a vault in Oak Ridge Cemetery. His body was finally moved to the tomb in 1871, though it would not be completed until 1874.",
          "width": 3648,
          "height": 2736,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Teemu008 from Palatine, Illinois",
